-- תחום תנאי שירות עובדי הוראה — שאלות ותשובות
-- The ministry's answers on fourteen topics. They are its reading, not
-- binding law: each answer the takanon's L4 can decide is checked here
-- against the takanon sections, IMPORTed and never copied. Where the
-- takanon's encoding agrees, the #ASSERT holds; where it disagrees, or the
-- takanon is silent and the answer adds a rule, the finding is in this
-- page's findings file and its boolean is #ASSERTed TRUE below.
-- (The `takanon-<section>` modules are links to the section files.)

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `takanon-1-9`
IMPORT `takanon-1-10`
IMPORT `takanon-1-11`
IMPORT `takanon-1-12`
IMPORT `takanon-1-13`
IMPORT `takanon-1-23`
IMPORT `takanon-1-25`
IMPORT `takanon-1-28`
IMPORT `takanon-1-46`
IMPORT `takanon-4-6`
IMPORT `takanon-7-6`

§ `שאלות ותשובות`

-- akn:hc_1/p1 The portal's breadcrumb and the page title; no rule.
-- akn:hc_1/p2 akn:hc_1/p3 akn:hc_1/p4 akn:hc_1/p5 akn:hc_1/p6 akn:hc_1/p7 akn:hc_1/p8 akn:hc_1/p9 akn:hc_1/p10 akn:hc_1/p11 akn:hc_1/p12 akn:hc_1/p13 akn:hc_1/p14 akn:hc_1/p15 akn:hc_1/p16 The page's list of topics, each a heading over the answers below.

§§ `גמול פיצול`

-- akn:hc_1/p17 The topic heading; the answers follow.

-- Q1: two subjects in 3 classes is not 6 classes; "a class" is a home
-- class. The takanon (section 1.11.1א) counts "כיתות" taught, and its L4
-- counts every group taught: the same class taught two subjects is two, a
-- reading the takanon does not make (F-1.11-f).
@ref akn:hc_1/p18 akn:hc_1/p19
GIVEN `home classes taught` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the answer counts enough home classes` `home classes taught` IF
    `home classes taught` AT LEAST 6

`two subjects in three classes` MEANS
    `a teacher's year with`
        (LIST `an eighth-grade class`, `an eighth-grade class`, `an eighth-grade class`,
              `an eighth-grade class`, `an eighth-grade class`, `an eighth-grade class`)
        1 1

`the takanon counts two subjects in three classes as six and the answer as three` MEANS
        `classes counted` `two subjects in three classes` EQUALS 6
    AND `qualifies under 1א` `two subjects in three classes`
    AND (NOT `the answer counts enough home classes` 3)

-- Q2: a class accompanied in a project does not count; only a class (or a
-- grouping from two classes) where the teacher teaches a subject on the
-- supervision's list of recognised subjects. The takanon names no list of
-- subjects: a whole class taught counts whatever is taught in it.
@ref akn:hc_1/p20 akn:hc_1/p21
GIVEN `teaches a subject the supervision recognises` IS A BOOLEAN, g IS A `taught group`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the answer counts the class` `teaches a subject the supervision recognises` g IF
    `teaches a subject the supervision recognises` AND `counts as a class under 2א` g

`the takanon counts a class whatever subject is taught in it` MEANS
        `counts as a class` `an eighth-grade class` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2003)
    AND (NOT `the answer counts the class` FALSE `an eighth-grade class`)

-- Q3: a class one only educates, teaching no subject in it, is not
-- counted: the instructions say "המלמד". The takanon's count is of groups
-- TAUGHT, so such a class is not among them: five taught classes and one
-- educated only do not reach six. The answer and the takanon agree.
@ref akn:hc_1/p22 akn:hc_1/p23
`five taught classes and one educated only` MEANS
    `a teacher's year with`
        (LIST `an eighth-grade class`, `an eighth-grade class`, `an eighth-grade class`,
              `an eighth-grade class`, `an eighth-grade class`)
        1 1
#ASSERT NOT `qualifies under 1א` `five taught classes and one educated only`

-- Q4: on 30/24 hours (125%), six classes qualify only if they fall within
-- 24 of the 30 hours — "בגבולות משרה אחת". In section 1.11.1א that phrase
-- qualifies the third alternative (three institutions), not the classes
-- (F-1.11-c); the takanon's L4 counts six classes on any position.
@ref akn:hc_1/p24 akn:hc_1/p25
GIVEN `classes within one position` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the answer's six classes within one position` `classes within one position` IF
    `classes within one position` AT LEAST 6

-- Six classes on 30/24 hours, only five of them within the first 24.
`six classes on 125%, five within one position` MEANS
    `a teacher's year with`
        (LIST `an eighth-grade class`, `an eighth-grade class`, `an eighth-grade class`,
              `an eighth-grade class`, `an eighth-grade class`, `an eighth-grade class`)
        1.25 1

`the takanon pays six classes beyond one position and the answer does not` MEANS
        `qualifies under 1א` `six classes on 125%, five within one position`
    AND (NOT `the answer's six classes within one position` 5)

-- Q5: matriculation-preparation hours (and education and grant hours) are
-- teaching hours, but "one position" for the split counts only frontal
-- hours. The takanon says which classes count (section 1.11.5ד counts those
-- prepared for matriculation) and never which hours make up the "one
-- teaching position" of section 1.11.1א: the outcome turns on a count it
-- does not define. Three institutions, 24 frontal hours and 3 hours of
-- matriculation preparation on a 24-hour base:
@ref akn:hc_1/p26 akn:hc_1/p27
`three institutions, 24 frontal hours and 3 preparation hours, counted with them` MEANS
    `a teacher's year with` EMPTY (27 DIVIDED BY 24) 3
`three institutions, 24 frontal hours and 3 preparation hours, counted without them` MEANS
    `a teacher's year with` EMPTY (24 DIVIDED BY 24) 3

`the third alternative turns on hours the takanon does not count` MEANS
        `qualifies by institutions only within one position` `three institutions, 24 frontal hours and 3 preparation hours, counted without them`
    AND (NOT `qualifies by institutions only within one position` `three institutions, 24 frontal hours and 3 preparation hours, counted with them`)

§§ `הוצאות נסיעה`

-- akn:hc_1/p28 The topic heading; the answers follow.

GIVEN pass IS A BOOLEAN, days IS A NUMBER, `some days only` IS A BOOLEAN, price IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `commuting month`
DECIDE `a commuting month with` pass days `some days only` price IS
    `commuting month` WITH
        `a free monthly pass operates where the employee lives` IS pass
        `passes the journey needs`                IS 1
        `price of a monthly pass`                 IS price
        `days employed a week`                    IS days
        `real travel expenses of the month`       IS 90
        `needs transport to reach work`           IS TRUE
        `published allowance for a full month`    IS 250
        `published allowance per journey`         IS 6
        `required to attend only some days`       IS `some days only`
        `journeys made`                           IS 32
        `in a month after the first of a continuous paid absence longer than a month` IS FALSE
        `in a month after the first of reserve duty longer than a month` IS FALSE
        `on unpaid leave`                         IS FALSE
        `work temporarily stopped`                IS FALSE
        `a month of the summer break`             IS FALSE

-- Q1 (a city with a free monthly pass): two days a week, real expenses —
-- the takanon agrees (section 1.9.1א ¶4). More than two days: the pass's
-- price "יחסית למספר ימי עבודתך". The takanon pays the price of the pass
-- without deduction (1א ¶2), and where attendance is required on some days
-- only, the published allowance per journey (1ב.3, by F-1.9-a's reading):
-- it never pays a share of the pass's price. Figures are placeholders.
@ref akn:hc_1/p29 akn:hc_1/p30
GIVEN `price of the pass` IS A NUMBER, `days worked a week` IS A NUMBER, `days of the school week` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the answer's share of the pass` `price of the pass` `days worked a week` `days of the school week` IS
    `price of the pass` TIMES `days worked a week` DIVIDED BY `days of the school week`

-- The two-day case is 1א ¶4's own rule, "בכל מקרה": real expenses, ahead
-- of the per-journey rule even where she attends on those days only.
#ASSERT `commuting allowance` (`a commuting month with` TRUE 2 TRUE 200) EQUALS 90

`the takanon's allowance for a four-day pass user does not follow the pass's price` MEANS
        `pass user's allowance` (`a commuting month with` TRUE 4 TRUE 200)
            EQUALS `pass user's allowance` (`a commuting month with` TRUE 4 TRUE 400)
    AND (NOT (`the answer's share of the pass` 200 4 6 EQUALS `the answer's share of the pass` 400 4 6))

-- Q2: one who comes daily from outside the city by car is paid the real
-- expenses at the public-transport fare. The takanon pays real bus fares
-- to one POSTED outside the jurisdiction for the system's needs (section
-- 1.9.1.2א); otherwise, the comptroller's published allowance, by bus or
-- by car alike (1ב.1). The answer pays the fare without the posting.
@ref akn:hc_1/p31 akn:hc_1/p32
`a teacher who chose to work outside the city` MEANS
    `work outside the jurisdiction` WITH
        `posted there for the system's needs`           IS FALSE
        `moved home out of the jurisdiction`            IS FALSE
        `the move raised the travel expenses or first made them payable` IS FALSE
        `moved at the Ministry's demand`                IS FALSE
        `moved for personal reasons the committee recognised` IS FALSE
        `in official education`                         IS TRUE
        `asked for a transfer and the Ministry agreed`  IS FALSE
        `the transfer took the workplace further from home` IS FALSE
        `moved to another city and still works in the old one` IS FALSE
        `asked for work in the new city and was not placed for two years` IS FALSE
        `a realistic placement in the new city was not used` IS FALSE
        `real bus fares for the days travelled`         IS 300
        `allowance before the move`                     IS 0
        `allowance at the previous workplace`           IS 0
        `allowance on the present journey`              IS 250

`the takanon pays real fares only to one posted outside the city` MEANS
        (NOT `paid real bus fares as posted` `a teacher who chose to work outside the city`)
    AND (NOT (`allowance outside the jurisdiction` `a teacher who chose to work outside the city` EQUALS 300))

-- A car user is paid as a bus user: the takanon too pays "בין אם הוא
-- משתמש בתחבורה ציבורית ובין אם הוא משתמש ברכב פרטי" (1ב.1) — the vehicle
-- changes nothing. The month's allowance does not read the vehicle at all.
#ASSERT `allowance without a pass` (`a commuting month with` FALSE 5 FALSE 0) EQUALS 250

§§ `וותק בניהול`

-- akn:hc_1/p33 The topic heading; the answer follows.

-- The supplement is computed on the management allowance due by the kind
-- of institution and the number of classes, not on the combined salary and
-- the 1994 supplement. The takanon says the same (section 7.6.10, its
-- note), and its L4 takes the allowance amount alone: 2.4% a year from the
-- second year. An allowance of 1,000 over five years (a placeholder):
@ref akn:hc_1/p34 akn:hc_1/p35
#ASSERT `management seniority addition` 1000 5 EQUALS 1000 TIMES 2.4% TIMES 4

§§ `חופשת הקיץ`

-- akn:hc_1/p36 The topic heading; the answer follows.

-- A teacher who did not work to the end of the year is entitled; the pay
-- follows the extent and the period of work; half a year, half the summer.
-- The takanon agrees (section 1.25.2.2א–ב): it asks more than 51
-- consecutive workdays and two months taught, not work up to the summer,
-- and its quota is per month of work. The daily salary of 100 is a
-- placeholder.
@ref akn:hc_1/p37 akn:hc_1/p38
GIVEN months IS A NUMBER, `months on paid sick leave` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `summer case`
DECIDE `an elementary teacher's year of` months `months on paid sick leave` IS
    `summer case` `kindergartens and elementary institutions` `on the permanent staff`
        (months TIMES 18) months (months MINUS `months on paid sick leave`) 0 0 1 100

`half a year earns half the summer` MEANS
    `summer-vacation pay` (`an elementary teacher's year of` 5 0)
        EQUALS `summer-vacation pay` (`an elementary teacher's year of` 10 0) DIVIDED BY 2
#ASSERT `half a year earns half the summer`

-- The answer counts paid sick leave as work for the summer. The takanon
-- counts maternity leave (2.6) and an injury on a trip (2.8), and no
-- paragraph of section 1.25.2 counts sick leave: five months taught, two of
-- them on paid sick leave, earn three months' summer under its L4.
`the takanon's summer does not count paid sick leave as work` MEANS
    `months of work for the summer` (`an elementary teacher's year of` 5 2) EQUALS 3

§§ `חופשת חגים`

-- akn:hc_1/p39 The topic heading; the answers follow.

-- Q1: a Jewish teacher in an Arab institution, or an Arab teacher in a
-- Jewish one, has paid leave on the fixed holidays of his religion AND on
-- those of his workplace. The takanon's holiday rules (section 1.25.1) pay
-- the vacation in the ministry's published calendar for the institution;
-- no paragraph speaks of the teacher's own religion.
@ref akn:hc_1/p40 akn:hc_1/p41
DECLARE `calendar of holidays` IS ONE OF
    `the workplace's holidays`
    `the teacher's own religion's holidays`

`the calendars the takanon's holiday rules pay` MEANS LIST `the workplace's holidays`
`the calendars the answer pays` MEANS
    LIST `the workplace's holidays`, `the teacher's own religion's holidays`

`the answer pays holidays no takanon rule pays` MEANS
    any (GIVEN c YIELD NOT elem c `the calendars the takanon's holiday rules pay`) `the calendars the answer pays`

-- Q2: a teacher on sick or maternity leave on the eve of the holiday is
-- paid for it: paid sick days and maternity leave paid by national
-- insurance count as workdays. The takanon agrees (section 1.25.1,
-- entitlement 1, second paragraph).
@ref akn:hc_1/p42 akn:hc_1/p43
GIVEN `the day before` IS A `kind of day before the holiday`, `unpaid leave after` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `holiday case`
DECIDE `a permanent teacher whose last day was` `the day before` `unpaid leave after` IS
    `holiday case` WITH
        `status for the holiday`                       IS `on the permanent staff`
        `last day before the holiday`                  IS `the day before`
        `on unpaid leave after the holiday`            IS `unpaid leave after`
        `the unpaid leave before was approved by the Ministry` IS FALSE
        `days of substitution`                         IS 0
        `workdays before the vacation`                 IS 0
        `days of the holiday vacation`                 IS 8
        `returned to work the day after the vacation`  IS FALSE
        `months worked before the vacation`            IS 0
        `work ended with the end of studies before the holiday` IS FALSE
        `the returning permanent employee is entitled` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `paid for the holiday vacation` (`a permanent teacher whose last day was` `paid sick leave` FALSE)
#ASSERT `paid for the holiday vacation` (`a permanent teacher whose last day was` `maternity leave paid by national insurance` FALSE)

-- But the answer's rule is "רק אם עבד לפני ואחרי החג". The takanon's rule
-- for the permanent staff is work BEFORE the holiday; after it, only unpaid
-- leave disqualifies (the note). A permanent teacher who worked before and
-- did not return after — absent, not on unpaid leave, and not returning
-- the day after — is paid by the takanon and not by the answer.
GIVEN `worked before` IS A BOOLEAN, `worked after` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the answer pays the holiday` `worked before` `worked after` IF
    `worked before` AND `worked after`

`the takanon pays a permanent teacher who did not work after the holiday` MEANS
        `paid for the holiday vacation` (`a permanent teacher whose last day was` `a day of work` FALSE)
    AND (NOT `the answer pays the holiday` TRUE FALSE)

§§ `חופשת מחלה`

-- akn:hc_1/p44 The topic heading; the answers follow.

-- Q1: the redemption of unused sick days, on the yearly data of
-- entitlement and use with every employer, under section 1.25.3.2; the
-- worked example: 594 days earned, 55 used.
-- akn:hc_1/p45 The question; the answer and its example are encoded below.
-- akn:hc_1/p46 A pointer to the conditions of section 1.25.3.2, applied below through its L4.
`the answer's retiree` MEANS
    `retirement case` WITH
        `how the service ended`            IS `retirement on pension`
        `age at retirement`                IS 65
        `years of permanent or temporary service` IS 20
        `left survivors`                   IS FALSE
        `months of service with a right to sick leave` IS 594 DIVIDED BY 2.5
        `sick days used in the whole service` IS 55
        `position fraction at retirement`  IS 1
        `monthly salary on the eve of retirement` IS 2500
        `days accumulated while working as a pensioner` IS 0

-- The share used, 55 of 594, is 9.26%; under 36%, so 8 days' pay for every
-- 30 days; the balance is 539; 539 × 8 / 30 is 143.7. The takanon agrees
-- with each step, and the answer's 143.7 is the pro-rata reading F-1.25-j
-- adopts (whole blocks of 30 would give 136).
@ref akn:hc_1/p47 akn:hc_1/p48 akn:hc_1/p49 akn:hc_1/p50
#ASSERT `share of sick leave used` `the answer's retiree` LESS THAN 0.36
#ASSERT `share of sick leave used` `the answer's retiree` GREATER THAN 0.0925
#ASSERT `share of sick leave used` `the answer's retiree` LESS THAN 0.0927
#ASSERT `days' pay for every 30 days of balance` `the answer's retiree` EQUALS 8
#ASSERT `balance of sick-leave days` `the answer's retiree` EQUALS 539
#ASSERT `days' pay of compensation` `the answer's retiree` GREATER THAN 143.7
#ASSERT `days' pay of compensation` `the answer's retiree` LESS THAN 143.75
#ASSERT `days' pay on the other reading, whole blocks of 30` `the answer's retiree` EQUALS 136

-- The answer then pays 144 days: "143.7 (144)". The takanon says nothing
-- of rounding the days' pay, and its L4 pays 143.7.
@ref akn:hc_1/p51
`the answer's days' pay` MEANS 144

`the answer rounds the days' pay and the takanon does not` MEANS
    NOT (`days' pay of compensation` `the answer's retiree` EQUALS `the answer's days' pay`)

-- The payment: the salary that determines the PENSION, for 100% of a
-- position, times 144 over 25. The takanon's day's pay is 1/25 of the
-- "monthly salary" on the eve of retirement, which it defines as the
-- combined salary and the additions counted for SEVERANCE (section
-- 1.25.3.2.6, citing 1.28.2), paid by the actual extent of the position,
-- above one included (paragraphs 4 and 5).
@ref akn:hc_1/p52 akn:hc_1/p53 akn:hc_1/p54 akn:hc_1/p55
DECLARE `salary a day's pay is taken of` IS ONE OF
    `the salary that determines the pension`
    `the combined salary and the additions counted for severance pay`

`the salary the takanon names` MEANS `the combined salary and the additions counted for severance pay`
`the salary the answer names` MEANS `the salary that determines the pension`

`the answer and the takanon name different salaries for a day's pay` MEANS
    NOT (`the salary the takanon names` EQUALS `the salary the answer names`)

-- The position: the answer pays for 100% because the days were counted in
-- full-position terms; the takanon multiplies by the position at
-- retirement. A retiree at half a position, the rest as above:
`the answer's retiree at half a position` MEANS
    `retirement case` WITH
        `how the service ended`            IS `retirement on pension`
        `age at retirement`                IS 65
        `years of permanent or temporary service` IS 20
        `left survivors`                   IS FALSE
        `months of service with a right to sick leave` IS 594 DIVIDED BY 2.5
        `sick days used in the whole service` IS 55
        `position fraction at retirement`  IS 0.5
        `monthly salary on the eve of retirement` IS 2500
        `days accumulated while working as a pensioner` IS 0

`the takanon scales by the position at retirement and the answer pays a full position` MEANS
    `compensation for unused sick leave` `the answer's retiree at half a position` FALSE
        EQUALS `compensation for unused sick leave` `the answer's retiree` FALSE DIVIDED BY 2

-- Q2: ill from mid-year on 125% as a class educator, paid on sick days by
-- the same data to the end of that year; the next year the components that
-- are not permanent are taken off, so 100% and no education allowance. The
-- takanon pays on sick leave "what would have been earned working"
-- (section 1.25.3.1, clause 1ג) and says nothing of a second year or of
-- tenure: its L4 passes the salary through as it is.
@ref akn:hc_1/p56 akn:hc_1/p57
GIVEN `salary of the year the illness began` IS A NUMBER, `permanent part of it` IS A NUMBER, `a later school year` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the answer's sick pay` `salary of the year the illness began` `permanent part of it` `a later school year` IS
    IF `a later school year` THEN `permanent part of it` ELSE `salary of the year the illness began`

`the takanon keeps the salary the answer cuts in the next year` MEANS
        `salary on sick leave` 12500 EQUALS 12500
    AND `the answer's sick pay` 12500 10000 TRUE EQUALS 10000

§§ `ליווי טיולים`

-- akn:hc_1/p58 The topic heading; the answer follows.

-- A teacher in two schools, away from school A to accompany school B's
-- trip: A deducts those days, and B pays him as one accompanying on a free
-- day. The takanon's second half agrees: one accompanying on a day he does
-- not teach is paid 4 hours more (section 1.10, ט). Of the first half — a
-- school deducting the days its teacher was away with another school's
-- trip — no paragraph of the takanon speaks.
@ref akn:hc_1/p59 akn:hc_1/p60
#ASSERT `extra hours for accompanying on a rest or non-teaching day` 0 EQUALS 4

DECLARE `trip-day consequence` IS ONE OF
    `school A deducts the day`
    `school B pays the accompanying on a free day`

`the consequences the takanon states` MEANS LIST `school B pays the accompanying on a free day`
`the consequences the answer states` MEANS
    LIST `school A deducts the day`, `school B pays the accompanying on a free day`

`the answer deducts a day no takanon rule deducts` MEANS
    any (GIVEN c YIELD NOT elem c `the consequences the takanon states`) `the consequences the answer states`

§§ `מורה אם`

-- akn:hc_1/p61 The topic heading; the answers follow.

-- Q1: at 79% or more with one employer, the employer pays the 10%
-- AUTOMATICALLY, by the family status in its questionnaires. The takanon
-- pays on a REQUEST made through the principal; a request made later is
-- approved from the month after it (section 1.13, הוראות ביצוע 1). A
-- teacher entitled from month 3 who asks in month 5:
@ref akn:hc_1/p62 akn:hc_1/p63
`the answer's first month paid` MEANS 3

`the takanon pays from the request and the answer from the entitlement` MEANS
    NOT (`first month paid` 3 5 EQUALS `the answer's first month paid`)

-- Q1, second paragraph: a teacher at two owners, under 79% at each, tells
-- each at the start of the year how much she works at the other. The
-- takanon asks the same of a part-time teacher in several institutions
-- (section 1.13, הוראות ביצוע 2, last sentence): a declaration of her
-- hours in each, and a confirmation to each of her hours elsewhere, made
-- with the request she files on entering work (הוראות ביצוע 1).
@ref akn:hc_1/p64
DECLARE `two-owner action` IS ONE OF
    `tell each owner her employment at the other`

GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `two-owner action`
DECIDE `telling each owner at the start of the year` IS
    PARTY `the teaching employee`
    MUST  `tell each owner her employment at the other`
    WITHIN 1
    LEST  BREACH BY `the teaching employee` BECAUSE "the answer: at the start of the school year, each owner is told her employment at the other"

-- The takanon's duty reaches the same teacher: part-time, in two places.
#ASSERT `declares her hours institution by institution` TRUE 2

-- Q2 and Q4: under 79% at one owner and 79%–140% in all, she is entitled,
-- and each owner pays in proportion. The supplement is "10% מהשכר ל-100%
-- משרה": 80% is paid as 90%, 90% as 100%. Example: 50% and 40%, 90% in
-- all, paid as 100%; owner A pays 10% × 50/90, owner B 10% × 40/90. The
-- takanon gives "תוספת בשיעור 10% לשכרה המשולב" — 10% of HER salary — and
-- its L4 has each owner pay 10% of its own share: 5% and 4%, 9% of a
-- position in all. The combined salary of 10,000 is a placeholder.
@ref akn:hc_1/p65 akn:hc_1/p66 akn:hc_1/p67 akn:hc_1/p68 akn:hc_1/p72 akn:hc_1/p73
GIVEN `full-position salary` IS A NUMBER
      shares IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
DECIDE `the answer's supplement by owner` `full-position salary` shares IS
    map (GIVEN s YIELD 10% TIMES `full-position salary` TIMES s DIVIDED BY sum shares) shares

`the takanon's 50% and 40%` MEANS
    `supplement paid by each owner` (`a mother's year with` (LIST `hours of` 0.5 0, `hours of` 0.4 0))

#ASSERT sum (`the answer's supplement by owner` 10000 (LIST 0.5, 0.4)) EQUALS 1000

`the takanon pays 10% of her salary and the answer 10% of a full position` MEANS
        `the takanon's 50% and 40%` EQUALS LIST 500, 400
    AND (NOT (sum `the takanon's 50% and 40%` EQUALS sum (`the answer's supplement by owner` 10000 (LIST 0.5, 0.4))))

-- Q2, last paragraph: at 79% or more with one owner, 10% from that owner
-- only, nothing from another. The takanon agrees (section 1.13.4).
@ref akn:hc_1/p69
#ASSERT `supplement paid by each owner` (`a mother's year with` (LIST `hours of` 0.8 0, `hours of` 0.3 0)) EQUALS LIST 800, 0

-- Q3: a teacher whose right has ended cannot demand 10% more position; the
-- owner, if it can, had better add it. The takanon agrees there is no right:
-- with no child under 14 she is not a "mother-teacher" and is owed nothing.
-- The owner's addition is a permission, which no paragraph forbids.
@ref akn:hc_1/p70 akn:hc_1/p71
`a fifteen-year-old` MEANS
    `child` WITH
        `relation to the employee`        IS `own child`
        `age on 1 September`              IS 15
        `age now`                         IS 15
        `age when taken into foster care` IS 0
        `months in foster care`           IS 0

#ASSERT NOT `is a child up to 14 this year` `a fifteen-year-old`

DECLARE `position action` IS ONE OF
    `add 10% to her actual position`

GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `position action`
DECIDE `the owner may add to her position` IS
    PARTY `the local authority or owning body`
    MAY   `add 10% to her actual position`

§§ `מינויים וגמולים של בעלי תפקידים`

-- akn:hc_1/p74 The topic heading; the answers follow.

-- Q1: the counsellor's allowance is the full rate for the years of
-- counselling × counselling hours / 12; the takanon's formula is the same
-- (section 1.12.7). The example: a counsellor of 3 years, 7%, 6 hours.
@ref akn:hc_1/p75 akn:hc_1/p76 akn:hc_1/p77
`the answer's counsellor` MEANS
    `counsellor` WITH
        `holds a counselling licence`            IS TRUE
        `weekly counselling hours`               IS 6
        `full rate for the years of counselling` IS 7%

#ASSERT `counselling rate` `the answer's counsellor` EQUALS 3.5%

-- The base of each percentage allowance: "שכר משולב + 3% תוספת הסכם הוראה
-- 2001 + תוספת הסכם הוראה 1994" — 3,308 + 99 + 124 = 3,531. The takanon's
-- base (section 1.12, its paragraph on the base) adds the 5% of 2008 and
-- the 4% of 2011.
@ref akn:hc_1/p78
`the answer's base` MEANS
    LIST `the combined salary by grade and teaching seniority`, `the 3% supplement (2001 agreement)`,
         `the 1994 teaching supplement`

`the takanon's base has components the answer's lacks` MEANS
    any (GIVEN c YIELD NOT elem c `the answer's base`) `the components of the allowances' base`

-- The example's figures, on the answer's base: 3,531 × 7% = 247, and
-- 247 × 6 / 12 = 123.5. The takanon's formula on the same base gives
-- 123.585: the answer rounds the full allowance to whole shekels first.
@ref akn:hc_1/p79 akn:hc_1/p80 akn:hc_1/p81 akn:hc_1/p82 akn:hc_1/p83 akn:hc_1/p84
#ASSERT 3308 PLUS 99 PLUS 124 EQUALS 3531
#ASSERT `counselling allowance` `the answer's counsellor` 3531 GREATER THAN 123.5
#ASSERT `counselling allowance` `the answer's counsellor` 3531 LESS THAN 123.6

-- Q2: a counsellor IS entitled to the subject-and-qualifications
-- allowance; "רק" one who gets the education, management, guidance or
-- supervision allowance is not. The takanon agrees on the counsellor, and
-- bars SIX allowances: kindergarten coordination and teacher-instructor
-- too (section 1.12, its paragraph 4.1).
@ref akn:hc_1/p85 akn:hc_1/p86
#ASSERT `entitled to subject and qualifications` `none of these` FALSE

`the allowances the answer bars` MEANS
    LIST `class education held`, management, guidance, supervision

`the takanon bars allowances the answer's "only" leaves out` MEANS
        (NOT `entitled to subject and qualifications` `kindergarten coordination` FALSE)
    AND (NOT `entitled to subject and qualifications` `teacher-instructor` FALSE)
    AND (NOT elem `kindergarten coordination` `the allowances the answer bars`)
    AND (NOT elem `teacher-instructor` `the allowances the answer bars`)

§§ `מענק יובל`

-- akn:hc_1/p87 The topic heading; the answer follows.

-- In the year in which, by the payslip, teaching seniority in Israel and
-- IDF seniority come to 30. The takanon counts both (section 1.46.1), and
-- pays the grant "ובכל שנה לאחר מכן" to one of "30 שנה ומעלה"; its L4
-- entitles every year at or above the threshold. The answer names ONE
-- year, the one the sum EQUALS 30. (A State employee's 25 years, from
-- 2008, is outside the question the answer was asked.)
@ref akn:hc_1/p88 akn:hc_1/p89
GIVEN seniority IS A NUMBER, `seniority in September of the year before` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `jubilee year`
DECIDE `a teacher's jubilee year with` seniority `seniority in September of the year before` IS
    `jubilee year` WITH
        `year of the grant`                          IS 2010
        `state employee on the teachers' scale`      IS FALSE
        `periods`                                    IS LIST
            (`period of service` `teaching` (seniority MINUS 3) FALSE),
            (`period of service` `military service` 3 FALSE)
        `seniority set in September of the year before` IS `seniority in September of the year before`
        `determining salary`                         IS 10000
        `position fraction that year`                IS 1
        `share of the year employed`                 IS 1
        `a pensioner`                                IS FALSE

GIVEN `seniority on the payslip` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the answer's jubilee year` `seniority on the payslip` IF
    `seniority on the payslip` EQUALS 30

#ASSERT `entitled to the jubilee grant` (`a teacher's jubilee year with` 30 29)

`the takanon pays the grant again a year after the answer's one year` MEANS
        `entitled to the jubilee grant` (`a teacher's jubilee year with` 31 30)
    AND (NOT `the answer's jubilee year` 31)

-- "לפי הכתוב בתלוש המשכורת": the payslip carries the seniority set in
-- September, which is paragraph 4's measure. F-1.46-a: paragraph 4 and ב
-- fix the year differently, and the takanon's L4 reads ב's 1 June count.
-- A teacher whose payslip says 29 and who completes 30 by 1 June is paid
-- by the takanon's reading and not by the answer's.
`the answer reads the payslip where the takanon reads 1 June` MEANS
        `entitled to the jubilee grant` (`a teacher's jubilee year with` 30 29)
    AND (NOT `the answer's jubilee year` 29)

§§ `קצובת ביגוד`

-- akn:hc_1/p90 The topic heading; the answer follows.

-- Is the clothing allowance part of the pension, severance pay and the
-- study-fund contributions? Budgetary pension: yes; accrued pension: no.
-- For severance pay the takanon agrees: "1/12 קצובת ביגוד (אך ורק
-- למבוטחים בפנסיה תקציבית)" (section 1.28.2.3, 2יד). For the pension and
-- the study fund no paragraph says either.
@ref akn:hc_1/p91 akn:hc_1/p92 akn:hc_1/p93
#ASSERT elem "1/12 of the clothing allowance (budgetary pension only)" (`the components counted on` 20100101)

DECLARE `use of the clothing allowance` IS ONE OF
    `clothing in severance pay`, `clothing in the pension`, `clothing in the study-fund contributions`

`the uses the takanon decides for clothing` MEANS LIST `clothing in severance pay`
`the uses the answer decides for clothing` MEANS
    LIST `clothing in severance pay`, `clothing in the pension`, `clothing in the study-fund contributions`

`the answer decides uses of the clothing allowance the takanon does not` MEANS
    any (GIVEN u YIELD NOT elem u `the uses the takanon decides for clothing`) `the uses the answer decides for clothing`

§§ `קרנות השתלמות`

-- akn:hc_1/p94 The topic heading; the answer follows.

-- Must the employer contribute? The answer: the contributions rest on a
-- collective agreement; to exercise the right the teacher fills in forms
-- and asks to join; the right is the teacher's. The takanon's regular
-- track has EVERY teaching employee pay monthly through the employer
-- (section 1.26.3, 1א–ב: "ישלם כל עובד הוראה"), with no application to
-- join.
@ref akn:hc_1/p95 akn:hc_1/p96
DECLARE `who joins the regular track` IS ONE OF
    `every teaching employee`
    `a teaching employee who applied to join`

`whom the takanon's regular track takes in` MEANS `every teaching employee`
`whom the answer's regular track takes in` MEANS `a teaching employee who applied to join`

`the answer asks for an application the takanon does not` MEANS
    NOT (`whom the takanon's regular track takes in` EQUALS `whom the answer's regular track takes in`)

-- The employer must contribute and cannot refuse; the owners, budgeted by
-- the ministry, must pass the money to the fund. The takanon agrees: the
-- employer passes the teacher's and its own share to the fund every month,
-- within a month of the salary (section 1.26.3, 1ב–ג, encoded there as an
-- obligation of the employer).
@ref akn:hc_1/p97 akn:hc_1/p98
DECLARE `fund action` IS ONE OF
    `pass the contributions to the fund`

GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `fund action`
DECIDE `the owner passes the contributions` IS
    PARTY `the local authority or owning body`
    MUST  `pass the contributions to the fund`
    WITHIN 1
    LEST  BREACH BY `the local authority or owning body` BECAUSE "the answer: the owner may not refuse to contribute and must pass the money to the fund"

§§ `שעות גיל`

-- akn:hc_1/p99 The topic heading; the answers follow.

-- Q1: from 24/24 to an age-hours base of 22: tenure is on the share of a
-- position, not on hours, so 22/22 is 100%. The takanon computes the
-- position the same way: hours over the base less the age hours (section
-- 1.23, paragraph 4). A teacher of 50, 22 hours on a base of 24:
@ref akn:hc_1/p100 akn:hc_1/p101
`a teacher of 50 on 22 of 24 hours` MEANS
    `age-hours case` 2024 1974 24 22 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 10000
#ASSERT `age hours` `a teacher of 50 on 22 of 24 hours` EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `position fraction for salary` `a teacher of 50 on 22 of 24 hours` EQUALS 1

-- Q2: a principal or deputy of 50 has the full age hours if he teaches 2/3
-- of his base: 16 hours on 24, 20 on 30. The takanon agrees (the managers'
-- paragraph of section 1.23).
@ref akn:hc_1/p102 akn:hc_1/p103
#ASSERT `managers' weekly reduction` (`manager's case` 2024 1974 TRUE 16 24) EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `managers' weekly reduction` (`manager's case` 2024 1974 TRUE 20 30) EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `managers' weekly reduction` (`manager's case` 2024 1974 TRUE 15 24) EQUALS 1

-- Q3: reaching 50 by 31 December, from the start of that school year; from
-- 1 January, from the next. The takanon agrees (paragraph 1). The school
-- year 2024 begins on 1.9.2024; born October 1974, and born January 1975:
@ref akn:hc_1/p104 akn:hc_1/p105
#ASSERT `reduction for 50` (`age-hours case` 2024 1974 30 28 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 10000) EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `reduction for 50` (`age-hours case` 2024 1975 30 28 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 10000) EQUALS 0

§§ `תוספת חינוך מיוחד`

-- akn:hc_1/p106 The topic heading; the answers follow.

GIVEN f IS A `special-education framework`, certified IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `special-education post`
DECIDE `a teacher in` f certified IS
    `special-education post` WITH
        `employed in a framework the supervision recognised as special education` IS f EQUALS `a special-education setting`
        `an integration kindergarten teacher`        IS FALSE
        `an integration teacher`                     IS f EQUALS `integration in regular education`
        `framework`                                  IS f
        `certified for special education`            IS certified
        `combined salary`                            IS 10000

-- Q1: the rate turns on certification and on the framework. The answer:
-- uncertified 5.5% integrated, 9% wholly special; certified 8.5%
-- integrated, 14% wholly special. The takanon (section 4.6.2–3): certified
-- 14% and 9%, uncertified 8.5% and 5.5%. Two of the four agree; the 9% and
-- the 8.5% are swapped.
@ref akn:hc_1/p107 akn:hc_1/p108
GIVEN f IS A `special-education framework`, certified IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the answer's rate` f certified IS
    CONSIDER f
    WHEN `a special-education setting`      THEN IF certified THEN 14% ELSE 9%
    WHEN `integration in regular education` THEN IF certified THEN 8.5% ELSE 5.5%
    WHEN `no special-education framework`   THEN 0

#ASSERT `special-education supplement rate` (`a teacher in` `a special-education setting` TRUE) EQUALS `the answer's rate` `a special-education setting` TRUE
#ASSERT `special-education supplement rate` (`a teacher in` `integration in regular education` FALSE) EQUALS `the answer's rate` `integration in regular education` FALSE

`the answer swaps the takanon's 9% and 8.5%` MEANS
        `special-education supplement rate` (`a teacher in` `a special-education setting` FALSE) EQUALS 8.5%
    AND `the answer's rate` `a special-education setting` FALSE EQUALS 9%
    AND `special-education supplement rate` (`a teacher in` `integration in regular education` TRUE) EQUALS 9%
    AND `the answer's rate` `integration in regular education` TRUE EQUALS 8.5%

-- Q2: every teacher in that framework is entitled, not only the class
-- educator. The takanon agrees: section 4.6 asks where one is employed, not
-- what role one holds there.
@ref akn:hc_1/p109 akn:hc_1/p110
#ASSERT `special-education supplement` (`a teacher in` `a special-education setting` FALSE) GREATER THAN 0

-- Q3: certified, but teaching in a regular framework this year — not
-- entitled. The takanon agrees.
@ref akn:hc_1/p111 akn:hc_1/p112
#ASSERT `special-education supplement` (`a teacher in` `no special-education framework` TRUE) EQUALS 0

-- And "יחסית להיקף העסקתו בחינוך המיוחד": in proportion to the share of
-- the employment in special education. The takanon's supplement is a rate
-- of the combined salary, with no share: one teaching half her hours in a
-- special setting is paid 14% of the whole salary by its L4, and half that
-- by the answer.
GIVEN rate IS A NUMBER, `combined salary` IS A NUMBER, `share in special education` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the answer's supplement` rate `combined salary` `share in special education` IS
    rate TIMES `combined salary` TIMES `share in special education`

`the takanon pays on the whole salary and the answer on the special-education share` MEANS
        `special-education supplement` (`a teacher in` `a special-education setting` TRUE) EQUALS 1400
    AND `the answer's supplement` (14%) 10000 0.5 EQUALS 700

-- akn:hc_1/p113 A pointer to section 1.26.1.2, sub-clause י, for one who does not work in special education at all.

§§ `Findings`

#ASSERT `the takanon counts two subjects in three classes as six and the answer as three`
#ASSERT `the takanon counts a class whatever subject is taught in it`
#ASSERT `the takanon pays six classes beyond one position and the answer does not`
#ASSERT `the third alternative turns on hours the takanon does not count`
#ASSERT `the takanon's allowance for a four-day pass user does not follow the pass's price`
#ASSERT `the takanon pays real fares only to one posted outside the city`
#ASSERT `the takanon's summer does not count paid sick leave as work`
#ASSERT `the answer pays holidays no takanon rule pays`
#ASSERT `the takanon pays a permanent teacher who did not work after the holiday`
#ASSERT `the answer rounds the days' pay and the takanon does not`
#ASSERT `the answer and the takanon name different salaries for a day's pay`
#ASSERT `the takanon scales by the position at retirement and the answer pays a full position`
#ASSERT `the takanon keeps the salary the answer cuts in the next year`
#ASSERT `the answer deducts a day no takanon rule deducts`
#ASSERT `the takanon pays from the request and the answer from the entitlement`
#ASSERT `the takanon pays 10% of her salary and the answer 10% of a full position`
#ASSERT `the takanon's base has components the answer's lacks`
#ASSERT `the takanon bars allowances the answer's "only" leaves out`
#ASSERT `the takanon pays the grant again a year after the answer's one year`
#ASSERT `the answer reads the payslip where the takanon reads 1 June`
#ASSERT `the answer decides uses of the clothing allowance the takanon does not`
#ASSERT `the answer asks for an application the takanon does not`
#ASSERT `the answer swaps the takanon's 9% and 8.5%`
#ASSERT `the takanon pays on the whole salary and the answer on the special-education share`

#TRACE `telling each owner at the start of the year` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the teaching employee` DOES `tell each owner her employment at the other` AT 1
#TRACE `the owner passes the contributions` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the local authority or owning body` DOES `pass the contributions to the fund` AT 1
